          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "No. The Hebrew word toda means acknowledgment before the outcome, not denial of pain. You can thank God while you hurt, while you are angry, while things look impossible. First Thessalonians 5:18 says in everything give thanks, not only in happy things. When you give thanks in the middle of the storm, you are not saying the storm is good. You are saying God is God and you trust His authority ahead of your feelings. This clarity is what thanksgiving gives you. It stops your emotions from locking you in the wilderness like it did the Israelites."
